+{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdMWnNbAHXZARwBBJE9ix","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three gates pass: **70/70 tests**, clean `tsc` build, zero lint errors (verified stable across 4 repeated test runs).\n\n## What I built\n\nEight service factories under `src/`, each returning its interface from `src/types.ts` and talking to the rest only through the bus:\n\n| Service | Notes |\n|---|---|\n| `catalog` | CRUD + name/category search; returns defensive copies so callers can't mutate internal state |\n| `inventory` | Stock ops routed through one `applyQuantity` helper that writes → emits `inventory:updated` → evaluates the reorder point |\n| `cart` | `createCart` deliberately does *not* emit; every mutation publishes full post-change contents |\n| `pricing` | Tax applies to the *discounted* subtotal; all money rounded to cents |\n| `orders` | Explicit `ALLOWED_TRANSITIONS` table; illegal transitions are a no-op with no event |\n| `payment` | Options for failure/timeout simulation; refunds reject unknown *and* already-refunded transactions |\n| `notifications` | Learns order→user mapping from `order:created`, since later order events only carry an `orderId` |\n| `analytics` | Counts, revenue, conversion, top products; banks revenue only when payment succeeds |\n\n## Two decisions worth flagging\n\n**`src/shared/emit.ts`** — I added one non-service module. Sync service methods return `void` by contract, so they can't await the bus; a throwing subscriber would surface as an unhandled rejection and take down the process. `emitAsync` isolates that. Async methods (`payment.processPayment`) instead `await bus.emit` directly and let errors propagate — the caller can handle them, and awaiting is what makes event propagation deterministic for callers. The file sits outside the eight service directories, so it doesn't violate the no-cross-service-imports rule.\n\n**Ordering determinism.** The riskiest